==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Violet Egg: N107''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cat Chief''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Cat Chief is a useful [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie Cat]] thanks to its potent combination of necessary abilities. The combination of Massive Damage vs. Zombies, Zombie Killer and inconsistent mini-waves all help in demolishing similarly low-ranged [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] peons. As one of the few universally accessible units with Soulstrike, this ability further augments its utility, since it can clear away Zombies before they revive if given enough time, preventing them from causing further trouble. It is especially devastating against Zombie-traited [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]] like [[Formicidaean Ariant]], finishing them in a couple of hits. However, its low range means its Behemoth Slayer is not useful elsewhere, and may have to rely on a stray Mini-Wave to snipe [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]], since Angaburu outranges Cat Chief and will have a hard time getting close due to his Slow ability on top of Mini-Surges inflicting it too.

Notably, Cat Chief competes with [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] for anti-Zombie utility. While Cadaver BearCat is much more disposable with significantly higher overall damage, Cat Chief has more knockbacks and survivability, is able to reach further with his greater range and can consistently deal with enemies outranging Cadaver BearCat like [[Zang Roo]], not to mention his Soulstrike. They can also be used together to cover each other's weaknesses.

